I'm not sure what kind of 'spatial values' you're looking for. If you're asking about (network) flow model measurements (e.g. shortest paths, , as it is called in combinatorial optimization problems (discrete math, linear optimization, integer optimization etc.), then you would need to apply linear/integer optimization solutions (e.g. shortest paths, p-medians, network partitioning etc.). Convexity, manifolds (e.g. locally Euclidean spaces) etc. cannot be assumed in such network flow settings ... Regards, Rudy

