> But the scaling is a likely problem, yes. If your space is in metres (default UTM coordinates, for example), then rescaling to kilometres is highly recommended.
> This would change the scale of E by a factor 1e6, so 1e8 would become a much more well-behaved 100.
>
> Finn
>
> On Fri, 31 Jul 2020 at 15:56, 'Colin Beale' via R-inla discussion group <r-inla-disc...@googlegroups.com> wrote:
> > Ah, this is very helpful. resp is either data from actual point locations (1) or 0 when background data. I have used 'e' to determine weight based on the area of the observation - for points this is zero, but for background data it indicase essentially the mesh resolution. I could rescale to coordinates to make this much smaller when non-zero if this will help, or I could have just miss-understood how this would work!
> >
> > Thanks!
> >
> > Colin
> >
> > On Friday, 31 July 2020 15:49:24 UTC+1, Helpdesk wrote:
